  {
    "id": "working-with-loop",
    "name": "Working with the Loop",
    "description": "Learn how the Loop panel, queue pausing, and the Health panel work together.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "title": "The Loop Panel",
        "markdownText": "**The Loop** runs a set of prompts automatically on a schedule or file-watch trigger.\n\nConfigure your loop in \u0060loop.md\u0060 \u2014 the Loop panel shows iteration status and lets you start, stop, or monitor progress.",
        "targetControlId": "LoopPanelBorder",
        "calloutPlacement": "East",
        "preAction": "None",
        "commandBefore": "",
        "commandAfter": "",
        "commandsBefore": null,
        "commandsAfter": null,
        "advanceTrigger": "",
        "targetOffsetX": 0.5,
        "targetOffsetY": 0.5
      },
      {
        "title": "Pausing the Queue",
        "markdownText": "**Pause the queue** to temporarily hold all pending prompts.\n\nThis is useful when you want to review the current agent\u0027s work before allowing the next queued item to run.",
        "targetControlId": "QueuePlayPauseButton",
        "calloutPlacement": "South",
        "preAction": "None",
        "commandBefore": "",
        "commandAfter": "",
        "commandsBefore": null,
        "commandsAfter": null,
        "advanceTrigger": "",
        "targetOffsetX": 0.5,
        "targetOffsetY": 0.5
      },
      {
        "title": "The Code Health Panel",
        "markdownText": "**The Code Health panel** runs configured checks against your codebase and reports results.\n\nUse \u0060code-health.md\u0060 to define which checks to run. Green = passing, red = action needed.",
        "targetControlId": "CodeHealthPanelBorder",
        "calloutPlacement": "East",
        "preAction": "None",
        "commandBefore": "",
        "commandAfter": "",
        "commandsBefore": null,
        "commandsAfter": null,
        "advanceTrigger": "",
        "targetOffsetX": 0.5,
        "targetOffsetY": 0.5
      }
    ]
  }
]